_output-jp-library/

# Local agent/memory tooling artifacts
.memsearch/
.claude/

# Agent working context: local-only, never committed.
#
# This previously read `_agent-context/*` followed by `!_agent-context/session-logs/`, which
# deliberately UN-ignored session logs and committed them to this repository. That contradicts the
# standing rule that session logs are local-only working notes: they carry machine paths, candid work
# narrative, and per-session detail that should not ship in a repository. The negation is removed
# (2026-08-12), so not-shipping-them is the default rather than something to remember per commit.
#
# It also had a concrete cost. Because the negation made those paths stageable, a `git add -A` in this
# repository swept a session log into a re-pin commit; it was caught before the PR existed, but the
# trap stayed armed. Staging re-pin files BY NAME is still the right habit, and now a slip is harmless.
_agent-context/

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
